ivileged  issues you show up you respond to that  subpoena you show up with counsel allow  counsel to raise the proper objections  preserve it for the court and then make  the appropriate ruling but you just  don't disregard a subpoena  if you do then you have to reap the  consequences i had a case before where i  subpoenaed a  law enforcement officer and this was a  virtual depot and he refused to turn on  his camera so i abruptly ended the  deposition i filed my appropriate motion  and my rule to show cause and a host of  officers in his defense showed up for  support but bottom line the judge made  its ruling you answer to that subpoena  and you follow the law so no one is  above the law seems like a procedural  issue that bannon's going to have a  similar issue with thank you for that  insight on that story when we come back  elaine maxwell is headed to federal  court we look ahead to the former  socialites trial and examine this week's  jury selection process  welcome back to law and crime daily a  lengthy jury selection is expected in  the trial of socialite elaine maxwell  accused of facilitating and  participating in sex crimes involving  minors this week a u.s federal judge  began screening more than 200 potential  jurors in the case 59 year old maxwell  is charged with six felonies including  conspiracy to entice minors to engage in  illegal sex acts and transportation of a  minor to engage in an illegal sex act  these charges stem from a relationship  with long-time companion jeffrey epstein  who was arrested on federal charges of  sex trafficking in 2019. federal  prosecutors say maxwell helped epstein  groom girls as young as 14 years old for  sexual abuse and sometimes participated  in the abuse maxwell pled guilty to all  charges and has been held without bond  in a brooklyn jail  the trial is set to begin on november  29th law and crime's adam classfeld will  be at the courthouse with the daily  updates  casey just a quick question she's pled  not guilty to those charges the judge is  questioning 200 prospective jurors to  get 50 qualified jurors to then get 12  jurors and six alternates after seeing  the written house and mcmichael and  brian trial how do you think selection  here will play out  well obviously the facts are totally  different however she is a socialite so  this is a high profile case the question  now becomes whether these allegations  the prosecution has sufficient evidence  to prove these allegations was she just  a socialite that was just doing or as  instructed by mr epstein a dead man  can't talk so it's her word against his  or did she know more so the prosecution  is going to have to tie those loose ends  together in order to prove beyond a  reasonable doubt that she was an active  participant and knew more than what  she's saying  makes a lot of sense in that aspect  terry what do you think are the  difficulties of jury selection in this  type of case against elaine maxwell  well like casey has said this is a very  high profile case  chances are all of the potential jurors  know about the case and they're going to  have their biases one way or the other  they're going to have very polarizing  issues in this case there are a lot of  people who are in support of the metoo  movement they're in support of the  time's up movement and they have their  opinions about that and when they go  through that vordier they're going to  have to ask very detailed questions i  expect that the questionnaire is going  to have specific questions about what do  they know about the case how are their  feelings about the metoo movement have  they ever been involved in this type of  case personally and they've probably all  heard about the weinstein and bill cosby  cases and that's something too that i  think is going to affect the jury  selection and so it's going to take time  and you're going to need people who have  time to deal with this long trial  absolutely and thank you both and thank  you for joining